// 官网「常见问题」的英文（#102，用户 11/28 21:47）：按 faq-default.js 的编号一条一条对应。
// /api/help?lang=en 只在这条跟默认内容一样时给英文（后台改过、新加的条目照样给中文）。
// 回答里能用的写法跟中文一样：**加粗**、[文字](/app 或 https://…)、以「- 」开头的行、空一行分段。
// 面板界面是中文的：菜单、按钮名后面括号里写原文，方便对照着找。
// 改中文 FAQ 的默认内容时，这里对应的一条也要改：zh 是那条中文问答的摘要（sha1 前 10 位），cloud/test/test_faq_en.mjs 会查对不上的。
export const FAQ_CATS_EN = { install: 'Installing', hosted: 'Hosting and renewal', login: 'Signing in and new phones', family: 'Family and permissions', proxy: 'Proxy and nodes', update: 'Updates', help: 'Feedback and contact' };

export const FAQ_EN = {
	"install-how": { zh: "ad1d6f715c", q: "How do I install it?", kw: "install command terminal setup start how to use", a: "1. Sign up on the [website](/app). Under Add router (添加路由器) → Install a new router (装新路由器), claim the free trial or redeem an invite code to get an install command\n2. Connect your phone to your home Wi-Fi, open the router admin (for example 192.168.1.1) → “Services” → “Terminal”, and sign in with root and your router password\n3. Paste the command and press Enter. When asked which edition to install, enter **1** for the AI edition or **2** for the local edition (home use only)\n4. Go back to My routers (我的路由器) on the website and tap Open panel (打开面板). No code needed. The local edition needs your home Wi-Fi" },
	"install-req": { zh: "4456b88bbc", q: "Will it run on my router?", kw: "supported model compatible flash space storage requirements 21.02 GL.iNet iStoreOS ucode", a: "You need **OpenWrt 22.03 or newer**. Kwrt, ImmortalWrt and similar builds all work. You also need about 2 MB of free flash.\n\nThe AI edition of the hosted service uses cloudflared (about 30 MB). If flash is short, the installer switches to downloading it into memory at boot, so it takes no flash. The local edition doesn’t use cloudflared.\n\nOn firmware such as OpenWrt 21.02 that ships an old ucode (some GL.iNet and iStoreOS builds, for example), since 5.2.3 the installer adds a dedicated runtime for the panel and leaves every original system file untouched." },
	"install-ver": { zh: "402620646a", q: "What is the difference between the AI and local editions?", kw: "Claude ChatGPT DeepSeek AI chat local edition panel only which one difference home only save space", a: "The hosted service comes in two editions. Accounts, family, push, cloud backup and one-tap updates are the same. The only difference is where you can open it:\n\n- **AI edition**: open the panel from anywhere (through a Cloudflare tunnel), and connect Claude, ChatGPT (developer mode), or apps that support MCP such as Cherry Studio with DeepSeek, Qwen and others\n- **Local edition**: opens only on your home Wi-Fi (`http://router-address:906/panel/`). It skips the tunnel program and saves about 30 MB of flash and tens of MB of memory compared with the AI edition. AI apps on a home computer still work, with the connector address changed to your home address\n\nTo switch later, use My page (我的主页) → This router (这台路由器) → Switch edition (换版本) in the panel, or My routers (我的路由器) → Switch edition (换版本) on the website. It is one tap and your settings are kept. Self-hosted installs still use the older “AI edition / Panel only” choice." },
	"edition-outside": { zh: "1d3df6f8bf", q: "I am away from home and the local edition won’t open. How do I switch to the AI edition?", kw: "away from home cannot open local edition switch AI edition app", a: "The local edition can’t be opened from outside, so switch it from your website account (only the main account can):\n\n- **Phone browser**: open My routers (我的路由器) on the website, tap Switch edition (换版本) → AI edition (AI 版) for this router, and enter the email code once\n- **Android app (6.0.2 and later)**: tapping a local-edition router while away shows Can’t open (打不开). Tap Switch to AI edition (换成 AI 版), or use ⋯ → Switch edition (换版本) on the router on the home screen\n\nThe router receives it within 3 minutes and you get a push when it is done. After that it opens from anywhere." },
	"edition-switch": { zh: "03bb979484", q: "How do I switch between the local and AI editions? What if it fails?", kw: "switch edition change local AI panel only failed rollback tunnel cloudflared", a: "Only the main account can switch, from either place:\n\n- **Panel**: My page (我的主页) → This router (这台路由器) → Switch edition (换版本), with progress for each step\n- **Website**: My routers (我的路由器) → Switch edition (换版本), after entering an email code once. The router receives it within 3 minutes and you get a push when it is done\n\n**Switching to local**: the website turns off the tunnel and the router removes cloudflared. Afterwards the panel won’t open from outside, only on your home Wi-Fi. “Open panel” on the website takes you straight to your home address with no password.\n\n**Switching to AI**: the router installs cloudflared (about 30 MB, kept in memory if flash is short) and the website sets up the tunnel. It takes about 2 minutes.\n\nIf any step fails (download error, not enough space, tunnel won’t connect), the router **automatically goes back to the previous edition** and keeps working. Both the panel and the website tell you which step failed and what to do, and the reason is reported to the developer.\n\nThe old hosted “Panel only” edition still works. You can turn on AI features in My page (我的主页) or switch it to the local edition." },
	"install-net": { zh: "2e63e6d35f", q: "Will installing cut my internet or break my settings?", kw: "offline internet impact settings backup risk", a: "No. The installer only adds the panel’s own programs and doesn’t touch your network or proxy settings. When you later edit rules and config files in the panel, the old version is backed up automatically before saving." },
	"install-fail": { zh: "4aec3b5082", q: "The install failed. What now?", kw: "failed error install problem report", a: "At the end the terminal asks whether to send a report. Enter **y** and press Enter. If you installed with an install code from the website, your account is recognized automatically, no email needed, and updates go to your account email.\n\nAfter reporting you get a ticket number. Enter it under “Check feedback status” at the bottom of the website to see the developer’s reply. The reply also appears at the top of the terminal the next time you run the install command." },
	"install-code": { zh: "843297bd62", q: "The install stopped halfway. Did I waste my install code?", kw: "install code invite code used up interrupted timeout reinstall wasted", a: "No.\n- If the network dropped, it timed out or you pressed Ctrl+C, run the install command again on the same router. The website hands out the previous activation result again without using another code\n- If activation failed on the website’s side, the code is returned automatically. Just install again\n- If it was activated but the router never connected to the website within 1 day (say you gave up halfway), the address is taken back and the code returns to your account\n- To reinstall after uninstalling, use the same install code. The expiry date stays the same (a reinstall doesn’t extend a trial). Once the hosted service has expired, the code can no longer be used to reinstall\n\nIf you see “This install code has already been used”, it is installed on a router right now. Each code works for one router, so get a new one under Add router (添加路由器) → Install a new router (装新路由器) on the website." },
	"install-un": { zh: "4046918781", q: "How do I uninstall?", kw: "uninstall remove delete stop using", a: "Enter `cmcp-uninstall` in the router admin terminal and press Enter. To wipe the settings completely afterwards, run the extra command shown in the terminal." },
	"install-self": { zh: "a22d76dcae", q: "Can I skip the hosted service?", kw: "self-hosted own domain Cloudflare LAN without website", a: "Yes. Use your own Cloudflare account and domain, or only your home LAN. All four self-hosted builds and guides are on [GitHub](https://github.com/wznwzn123/openwrt-claude-panel)." },
	"ai-clients-6": { zh: "e124ad3620", q: "Which AIs can I connect, and how?", kw: "AI ChatGPT Claude DeepSeek Qwen Kimi Cherry Studio MCP connector how to connect supported", a: "The AI edition’s “AI connector address” is a standard MCP connector (remote, Streamable HTTP, no sign-in), so any AI app that can add a remote MCP connector works. Copy the address from My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → AI connector address (AI 连接器地址) in the panel after verifying:\n\n- **Claude** (web and app): Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector, enter the address, no OAuth needed\n- **ChatGPT**: at [chatgpt.com/plugins](https://chatgpt.com/plugins) tap “+” → Add custom MCP server, enter the address and choose No authentication (your plan and workspace must allow custom connectors)\n- **Cherry Studio and other MCP clients** (which can use DeepSeek, Qwen, Kimi and other models): add an MCP server in settings, choose Streamable HTTP, enter the address, and turn the server on in your chat\n\nMenu names change from time to time, so go by what the app shows. Whichever AI you use, risky actions such as restarts, setting changes and installing or removing software only run after you tap Allow (允许) on your phone." },
	"ai-confirm-6": { zh: "108d5c1f38", q: "Why does the AI ask me to tap “Allow” on my phone? Can I turn that off?", kw: "Claude allow deny confirm read only risky action connector AI phone confirmation allow this kind allow everything revoke", a: "From 6.0 the AI connector defaults to “Confirm risky actions”. Viewing status, switching nodes and speed tests work as usual. To **restart the router, change settings, install or remove software, change proxy rules or run commands that change things**, the router first pushes the request to your phone (without push, it pops up when you open the panel on your phone). Check what it wants to do and tap Allow (允许). Approval lasts 5 minutes and covers one run. If Claude can’t wait for confirmation, it tells you to confirm on your phone and then tries again.\n\nRead-only commands (such as `cat`, `ls`, `logread`, `uci show`, `ping`) run right away without confirmation.\n\nYou can change this under My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → AI connector address (AI 连接器地址) after verifying it is you:\n- **Read only**: can view, can’t change anything\n- **Confirm risky actions** (recommended)\n- **Fully open**: like before 6.0, everything runs directly. If the connector address leaks, someone else can change things directly too\n\nThe main account and family members with “Full control” can tap “Allow”. If you didn’t ask the AI for it, tap Deny (拒绝) and change the connector address.\n\nThe small arrow next to “Allow” on the confirmation card has two more options:\n- **Allow this kind**: stops asking for that kind of action (for example running any command) and pushes a note to the main account. Revoke it from the “Allow this kind” list under “AI connector address”\n- **Allow everything**: the same as switching to “Fully open”. Only the main account can tap it, after verifying under My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) (no need again within 10 minutes). Change it back under “What the AI can do”" },
	"host-what": { zh: "dab9f81e5c", q: "What is the hosted service?", kw: "router address hosted what is remote access", a: "The hosted service gives each router its own address so you can open the panel from outside. It also includes push notifications, cloud backup and outage detection. No Cloudflare account or domain needed." },
	"host-restore": { zh: "b9c1886d55", q: "My router address won’t open and says suspended, expired or deleted. How do I get it back?", kw: "cannot open suspended expired deleted restore router address", a: "Your home internet and router settings aren’t affected. Only the address, push and cloud backup have stopped. From 6.0 the panel opened at the home address, the local edition and the AI connector are paused too, and the panel only shows status and accepts a renewal code. First open the [account page](/app) and see what it says for this router:\n\n- **Expired and paused**: tap Renew (续期) and enter a renewal code, or tap Request renewal (申请续期) and wait for review. It comes back as soon as it is renewed. If it stays paused for more than 30 days it is permanently deleted\n- **Suspended, restorable until a date**: contact the person who provides the service before that date. They can restore it with one tap in the admin page, and your old address and signed-in phones keep working\n- **The router is gone from your account** (or you got a “permanently deleted” email): get a new install code under Install a new router (装新路由器) on the account page and run the command there again. Settings are kept, the address changes" },
	"host-trial": { zh: "bef8a73d95", q: "My trial is about to end. What should I do?", kw: "trial expiry renew extend ending soon", a: "You get a push reminder 3 days before it ends. On the [account page](/app), tap Request renewal (申请续期) under the router and fill in the form. Once approved it renews automatically. If you have a renewal code, tap Renew (续期) and enter it. No reinstall needed." },
	"host-renew": { zh: "57b67a1c18", q: "How do I use a renewal code?", kw: "renewal code how to use enter redeem", a: "On the [account page](/app), under My routers (我的路由器), tap Renew (续期) below the router and enter the code. You can also tap Enter renewal code (输入续期码) under My page (我的主页) → Hosted service (托管服务) in the panel." },
	"host-status": { zh: "2cc8039ad6", q: "How can I tell whether the hosted service is having problems?", kw: "outage server down status your problem", a: "Check [Service status](/en/status): it shows whether each service is working right now, the last 90 days of history and any incident being handled." },
	"login-new": { zh: "761a1cb9f9", q: "I got a new phone or cleared my browser data. How do I sign in to the panel again?", kw: "new phone cleared data sign in login cannot open again", a: "Sign in to the [account page](/app) on the new phone and tap Open panel (打开面板) under My routers (我的路由器). No code needed." },
	"login-code": { zh: "52c97074bb", q: "How do I sign in to the panel when the website is down?", kw: "emergency sign-in code website down cmcp-logincode", a: "Run `cmcp-logincode` in the router admin terminal to get an emergency sign-in code, then enter it on the panel sign-in page. Signing in this way counts as the main account." },
	"login-lan": { zh: "94b429e804", q: "Can I open the panel at home without going through the website?", kw: "LAN local home direct 906 without website original admin intranet", a: "Yes (from 6.0). On a phone or computer connected to your home Wi-Fi, open `http://router-address:906/panel/` in a browser (for example `http://192.168.1.1:906/panel/`) and enter the router admin password once. That device is then remembered. The exact address is under My page (我的主页) → This router (这台路由器) → Open at home (在家里打开), tap to copy it.\n\n- **From the original admin**: after signing in to the original admin, tap Services (服务) → Router panel (路由器面板) with no extra password.\n- **Home only**: this address is open only on your home LAN, not from the internet or guest Wi-Fi. It doesn’t go through Cloudflare, so it works even when the website or the network has problems.\n- **Counts as the main account**: devices that come in this way can use every feature but can’t see website account details (renewals, family). Remove devices you don’t recognize under My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → Signed-in devices (登录着的设备) and change the router admin password.\n- If port 906 is taken it moves to 9906 or 19906. Go by what the panel shows." },
	"login-pw": { zh: "5f4a24631b", q: "I forgot my website password. What should I do?", kw: "forgot password reset change recover", a: "On the [account page](/app), tap Forgot password? (忘记密码？) below the sign-in box, get the code by email and set a new password. With two-step verification on, you also enter the authenticator code (or a backup recovery code) after setting the new password." },
	"tf-6": { zh: "6f7025496e", q: "How do I turn on two-step verification? What if I lose my phone?", kw: "two-step verification 2FA authenticator one-time code recovery codes backup codes lost phone", a: "From 6.0 website accounts can use two-step verification (optional). In [Account settings](/app#settings), tap Turn on (开启) under Two-step verification (两步验证), scan the code with an authenticator app on your phone (Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator or the built-in Passwords app on iPhone all work) and enter the 6-digit code it shows once.\n\n- **Once it is on**: signing in on a phone or computer that hasn’t signed in before needs the authenticator code after the right password (no more email codes). It is also needed after a password reset and to delete the account. Devices already verified need only the password for 30 days.\n- **Backup recovery codes**: you get 10 when turning it on, shown only once. Save them in a password manager or write them down. If you lose your phone, tap Use a backup recovery code (用备用恢复码) when signing in and enter one (each works once). Once in, you can generate a new set.\n- **Confirming it is you** (to view sensitive info and so on) also accepts the authenticator code, so you don’t have to wait for an email.\n- **Lost both the authenticator and the codes**: contact the service provider from your sign-up email. They turn it off once they confirm it is you.\n- **Turning it off**: tap Turn off (关闭) in [Account settings](/app#settings) and enter the authenticator code once." },
	"login-devs": { zh: "12c940e361", q: "Where can I see devices signed in to my account? Can I kick them out?", kw: "devices kick sign out unknown stolen sign-in log security", a: "- **Website account**: [Account settings](/app#settings) has Signed-in devices (登录着的设备). Sign out unknown ones individually or use Sign out all other devices (退出其他所有设备). An account can be signed in on up to 20 devices at once, and the oldest are signed out automatically\n- **Router panel**: My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → Signed-in devices (登录着的设备) in the panel shows which phones can open it. Remove any you don’t recognize\n\nWhen a new phone signs in to the panel, your signed-in phones get a push." },
	"login-wifi": { zh: "effabb1efc", q: "The panel won’t open on home Wi-Fi but works on mobile data?", kw: "Wi-Fi cannot open mobile data not loading spinning", a: "Usually the proxy plugin is restarting or a node is stuck. The panel switches to a direct route by itself, so wait a minute or two and refresh. If it is urgent, open it on mobile data first." },
	"login-mobile": { zh: "f652914e97", q: "The panel won’t open on mobile data when I am out unless I turn on a proxy?", kw: "mobile data outside cannot open proxy carrier relay cannot connect", a: "In some areas mobile networks can reach the website but not your router address. Since 5.2.3 the panel switches to a **relay through the website** by itself and tells you once when opening, no proxy needed. It tries the direct route again after 10 minutes.\n\nIf it still won’t open, the panel tells you which part is down: the phone has no internet, it can’t reach Cloudflare, or only the router address is down. The relay only forwards and stores nothing. See the [Privacy policy](/en/privacy)." },
	"login-app": { zh: "e0f30c76f0", q: "Is there a phone app?", kw: "app Android download home screen Apple iPhone", a: "There is an Android app, which you can download from the [home page](/en/). You can also open the panel in your phone browser and “Add to home screen”, which works just like an app." },
	"app-login": { zh: "d0a19ee2d1", q: "How do I sign in to my website account in the Android app?", kw: "app sign in login authorize sign in or sign up scan code password Android", a: "The app never takes your password directly, only authorization:\n- Tap Sign in or sign up (登录或注册). A website page opens inside the app (using your phone Chrome sign-in, so no need to sign in again if you already did). Tap Allow (允许) and you return to the app signed in. If you have no account yet, sign up on that page\n- Or tap Scan with a signed-in phone (用登录着的手机扫码) and confirm by scanning on another phone that is signed in to the website\n- When confirming, check which device it is and where. If it was not you, decline\n- The authorization code lasts 10 minutes and works once\n- In app versions 6.0.0 and 6.0.1 you confirm in the phone browser, then tap Back to app (回到 App) after “Allow”" },
	"app-switch": { zh: "77672c0c36", q: "How do I switch to another router or add one in the Android app?", kw: "app switch router change router multiple add router another home screen", a: "With only one router, the app opens straight into its panel. To switch or add another:\n- Tap Switch router (切换路由器) in the panel sidebar to go back to the app home screen (app 6.0.2 and later), or press back twice on the first panel page\n- The app home screen lists every router this phone has opened. Tap a row to open it, and use “⋯” to rename or remove\n- Use “+” at the top right to add one: sign in to your website account, scan a code, read a QR code from a photo, or paste or type a sign-in address\n- When using the hosted edition in a browser, “Switch router” in the sidebar opens “My routers” on the website" },
	"app-widget": { zh: "d66b212209", q: "Can I see my network speed on the Android home screen?", kw: "widget home screen speed Android", a: "Yes. From 6.0 the Android app has a home screen widget. Open the panel in the app, go to System (系统操作) → Home screen widget (桌面小组件) and tap Add (添加). It shows speed and the number of online devices. The system updates it every 30 minutes at most, and tapping it refreshes right away.\nIf tapping “Add” shows no prompt: on Xiaomi and Redmi phones, first turn on the “Home screen shortcuts” permission for the app and tap again, or long-press an empty spot on the home screen → “Widgets” → “路由器面板”.\nThe widget uses a key that can only read these few things. Remove it under My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → Signed-in devices (登录着的设备) when you no longer need it." },
	"app-lan": { zh: "ca0e83a7ce", q: "Can the app find my home router by itself?", kw: "LAN discovery find automatically home wifi app", a: "Yes (app 6.0 and later). Open the app on your home Wi-Fi and the router shows up under Found at home (在家里找到) on the home screen. Tap Open (打开) and sign in in the panel. It only finds the router and never signs in automatically." },
	"pass-6": { zh: "191cfa040b", q: "From 6.0, is the sign-in address still stored on my phone?", kw: "sign-in address key pass phone stored sign out copy", a: "No. The sign-in address is used only to get this phone its own key, after which the phone keeps none of the address’s secret. Normally each request carries a pass valid for 1 hour that renews automatically, so you won’t notice it.\n\n- Each phone’s key can be signed out on its own: My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → Signed-in devices (登录着的设备)\n- Keys renew every 12 hours. If someone copies an old key and uses it, this is detected, that phone is signed out and you get a push\n- Changing the sign-in key doesn’t sign out phones that are already signed in\n- Removing a phone or changing the sign-in key also changes the gate key used to open original pages from the panel. A removed phone can’t open original pages even with the old one, and other phones get the new one automatically\n- Self-hosted installs can also turn on “Require the router admin password to sign in”, so the sign-in address alone isn’t enough" },
	"bk-enc-6": { zh: "f1dced678c", q: "Are cloud backups encrypted? What if my router has no openssl?", kw: "backup encryption openssl ciphertext cloud old backups", a: "From 6.0 they are always encrypted: backups are encrypted on the router before upload, the key stays only on your router, and the cloud stores only unreadable ciphertext.\n\n- Routers with openssl use it, which is fast\n- Routers without openssl use the panel’s own encryption, nothing to install. On slower routers backups and downloads take a minute or two, and the panel shows progress\n- Old backups uploaded without encryption are replaced with encrypted copies at the next successful backup after upgrading. Their dates stay the same and they still restore\n- If encryption fails nothing is uploaded, and the panel explains why" },
	"guard-6": { zh: "d93e4c5863", q: "What if someone outside is guessing my router password?", kw: "block ban password guessing SSH admin sign-in alert internet security", a: "From 6.0 the panel handles it: 5 wrong router admin or SSH passwords from one public address within 10 minutes block that address for 1 hour (doubling on repeat, up to 1 day), and you get a push. Successful sign-ins also send a push saying where they came from.\n\n- Home devices and phones using the panel are never blocked (the panel goes through the router internally)\n- Blocked by mistake: tap Unblock (解封) under Features (特色功能) → Auto-block (自动拉黑) in the panel\n- Each of these alerts can be turned off separately under Features (特色功能)\n- The best protection is still a strong router password, and not exposing the admin and SSH to the internet if you don’t need them" },
	"lfull-6": { zh: "2efae6fb10", q: "Can I open the full router admin when I am away?", kw: "full admin original admin LuCI router password sign in outside", a: "Yes (from 6.0). Use Tools (工具) → Full original admin page (完整原版后台) in the sidebar to open the router admin (LuCI) as-is, and sign in with the router password just like at home.\n\n- Only phones signed in to this panel with “Full control” can see the sign-in page\n- 5 wrong router passwords in a row lock it for 15 minutes and send you a push. Every successful sign-in sends a push too\n- 30 minutes of inactivity signs you out. Tap Exit full admin (退出完整后台) at the top when you are done\n- Weak router passwords (under 8 characters, admin, 12345678 and the like) are refused. First set a strong one under System (系统) → Administration (管理权) → Router password (路由器密码)\n\nThe “original pages” you normally open in the panel still sign in automatically with no password." },
	"lock-6": { zh: "f8ba820c9b", q: "Do I have to enter the panel lock password every day?", kw: "panel lock fingerprint password daily unlock wrong attempts", a: "From 6.0 the router checks the panel lock password (it isn’t stored on the phone), so clearing site data doesn’t get around it.\n\n- **Password only**: enter it every time you reopen the panel or after the screen locks\n- **Fingerprint on**: unlock with your fingerprint normally. Fingerprints can only be checked on the phone, so the router asks for the password at least once a day\n- After 20 wrong attempts in total, the router signs that phone out and you need to sign in again" },
	"captcha": { zh: "402930d896", q: "Why do I have to tap a human check when signing in or signing up?", kw: "human check bot captcha tap not loading Turnstile", a: "Normally you never see it. It appears only when this device (or the same network) has made several attempts in a short time, or when the website is under attack protection, to stop mass password guessing and code spamming.\n\nOne tap and you continue, no information needed. If the check won’t load, switch networks (for example turn off Wi-Fi and use mobile data) or try again a bit later. Phones and computers already signed in, and the router itself, aren’t affected." },
	"mail-full": { zh: "51d8ddb291", q: "It says “Today’s email limit is reached, please try tomorrow”. What now?", kw: "verification code not received try tomorrow email limit cannot send", a: "The email service the website uses for codes has a daily sending limit, which is occasionally used up. When it is:\n\n- **Actions that need an email code** (signing up, resetting a password, signing in on a new device, confirming it is you) pause for the day and resume automatically the next day. Your account is fine, and verification isn’t skipped\n- **Problem reports, panel feedback and renewal requests** can still be sent and the developer sees them. Only the confirmation email is skipped that day. Track progress under My feedback (我的反馈) or on the account page\n\nPhones and computers that are already signed in keep working as usual." },
	"login-old": { zh: "ab1ac9f0c9", q: "The panel shows a blank screen on an old phone, or says the browser is too old?", kw: "blank screen cannot open browser too old WebView old phone Android 7", a: "The panel needs Chrome 64, Safari 12 or newer (browsers from 2018 onward). Before Chrome 84 a few spacings may look off. The Android app and many built-in phone browsers use Android System WebView, and if it is too old the panel won’t open.\n- Update Android System WebView or Chrome from the app store, then open the panel again\n- If you can’t update, open the panel address in Edge or Chrome\n- With a browser that is too old, the panel shows this message after 10 seconds instead of staying blank" },
	"back-gesture": { zh: "468b2694ed", q: "What happens when I swipe back or press the back button?", kw: "back swipe back button exit dialog gesture", a: "In the panel, the website and the admin console, swiping back, the Android back button and the computer browser’s back button all mean “go back one step”:\n\n- With a dialog or menu open, it closes first\n- If a dialog has unsaved input, you are asked before it closes\n- You go back to the page you were on rather than leaving\n\nOn Android, once you are back on the first page, one more back press exits (in the app it goes to the app home screen). On iPhone, after adding the panel to the home screen, swiping right from the left edge also goes back." },
	"fam-add": { zh: "aa680b3208", q: "My family wants to use it too. How do I add them?", kw: "family add people member join code share together", a: "Have them sign up on the [website](/app) first. In the panel, tap Add family member (添加家人) under My page (我的主页) → Family (家人) to create a join code and send it to them. They join with their own account and become a member. You choose what they can do item by item." },
	"fam-perm": { zh: "d4ed4b3e20", q: "What can each member permission do?", kw: "permissions what can they do full control proxy settings system view only", a: "- **View**: home, speed and outage log, for everyone. Devices and traffic depend on “See and manage all devices” below\n- **See and manage all devices**: without it, they can only see and manage devices assigned to them (off by default for family added from 6.0)\n- **Feedback and contact the developer**, **Switch nodes**, **Speed test**, **Parental controls** (pause internet and offline schedules, send a device direct, rename devices and change icons, delete offline devices), **Proxy settings** (rules, subscriptions, config), **System** (restart, services, panel updates)\n- **Full control**: open the router’s original admin, edit OpenClash custom scripts and overrides, restore backups. This makes them equal to the main account, so give it only to people you fully trust\n\nThe terminal, file manager, changing the sign-in key and hosted service settings are for the main account only." },
	"fam-full": { zh: "ccc635338e", q: "What does “Has full control” in the family list mean?", kw: "full control badge red has full control", a: "It means this family member can open the router’s original admin, edit scripts and restore backups, the same as the main account. Family members who previously had “Proxy settings” or “Network settings” are flagged automatically after upgrading. If you don’t want that, untick “Full control” under Manage (管理) and save." },
	"fam-own": { zh: "636ba1cf44", q: "How do I let a family member see only their own devices? Which devices count as theirs?", kw: "own devices only privacy owner claim my devices family hidden children", a: "Under My page (我的主页) → Family (家人) → Manage (管理), untick “See and manage all devices”. They then see and manage only devices assigned to them, and can’t see anyone else’s devices, traffic or connections. Family members who joined before 6.0 keep their old access (all devices), with a hint in the family list so you can decide whether to change it.\n\nWhich devices are theirs:\n- **Automatically**: the phone they open the panel with (if several people have the panel open at once this can’t be told apart, so use the two below)\n- **They claim it**: they tap Claim device (认领设备) on the “Devices” page and pick one, which counts once you tap Confirm (确认) at the top of the devices page\n- **You assign it**: More (更多) → Owner (归谁) on the device\n\nIf a device belongs to a child and you set its pause or internet schedule, the child can’t change it." },
	"fam-chat": { zh: "1aaa7f2d8c", q: "Can family members see my chats with the developer?", kw: "privacy chat see conversation history family", a: "No. Since v5.2.2, developer chat and feedback are separate for each person, and family members can’t see each other’s. Earlier conversations stay with the main account." },
	"fam-remove": { zh: "8d5940630c", q: "How do I suspend or remove a family member? Can I hand over the main account?", kw: "remove delete family suspend transfer main account change owner", a: "In the panel, tap Manage (管理) for the person under My page (我的主页) → Family (家人). You can suspend them, set an expiry date or remove them. Once suspended or removed, their phone can no longer open the panel.\n\nThe main account can tap Transfer main account (转让主账号) on the same page to hand it to another family member. After the transfer you become a member." },
	"fam-offline": { zh: "e887bff178", q: "Can family members still use it when the router can’t reach the website?", kw: "website unreachable offline family view only", a: "For the first 6 hours without the website, family members keep their usual permissions. After 6 hours they can only view, not change anything. The main account isn’t affected, and everything returns as soon as the website is back." },
	"px-plugins": { zh: "48439c708c", q: "I use a different proxy plugin. Will it work?", kw: "plugin OpenClash Nikki PassWall HomeProxy SSR supported", a: "Yes. OpenClash, Nikki, PassWall, PassWall2, HomeProxy and SSR Plus+ are all detected automatically. If you have two or more installed, switch between them with Proxy plugin · Switch (代理插件 · 切换) on the panel Overview (概览). Without a proxy plugin, devices, traffic, speed tests and the outage log still work." },
	"nikki-pages": { zh: "8d0ea450c7", q: "With Nikki, can I manage subscriptions, config files and rules in the panel?", kw: "nikki subscription config file profiles rules direct bypass mixin access control", a: "Yes, under Proxy (代理) in the sidebar:\n\n- Subscriptions: add, rename and change the address, update, check usage, delete, and switch with More (更多) → Use this subscription (使用这个订阅). The subscription address stays on the router, and the panel shows only the host name\n- Config files: your own files in /etc/nikki/profiles can be created, edited, switched and deleted. Before saving, Nikki’s core checks the format and the old version is backed up. Files downloaded by subscriptions and the running config are view-only, and subscription files can be saved as your own config to edit\n- Rules: Custom rules (自定义规则) are the rules you write in Nikki, one per line, such as DOMAIN-SUFFIX,douyin.com,DIRECT. A # at the start disables a line, and they come before subscription rules. Rules added by split routing are separate and managed on the Split routing (分流) page\n- Direct (no proxy): as with OpenClash, adding and removing take effect right away. It uses Nikki’s own access control and recognizes devices by MAC, so it still works after an IP change. In Nikki’s fake-ip mode a few sites may not open for a moment right after setting it, because the phone still remembers Nikki’s fake address. Wait a few seconds to a minute, or reconnect Wi-Fi if it is urgent\n\nSwitching subscriptions or config files and changing rules need a Nikki restart to take effect. The panel asks first, and only restarts when you tap Switch and restart (换并重启) or Save and restart (保存并重启). The internet drops for 10 to 30 seconds. If Nikki isn’t running, changes are only saved and used next time it starts. With both OpenClash and Nikki installed, the sidebar follows the one in use." },
	"px-auto": { zh: "410716ddca", q: "Does it switch nodes automatically when one breaks?", kw: "automatic switch node broken down auto fix proxy group", a: "Yes. The node in use is tested every minute (it only counts as down when both Google and Cloudflare test addresses fail). After 3 minutes of failures it switches automatically, pushes to your phone and writes which node it switched to and why in the outage log. A node that stalls for ten-odd seconds at peak time isn’t treated as dead.\n- It first tries nodes in the same region, of the same type and multiplier (dedicated line to dedicated line, 3x to 3x). If all of those are down it tries other nodes in the same region, and only then other regions. It understands the naming used by most providers: “专线 / IPLC / IEPL / 中转 / 家宽”, “3x / ×3 / 3倍”, “香港 / HK / 🇭🇰” and so on\n- When the original node recovers and stays healthy for 10 minutes, it switches back automatically, unless you switched nodes by hand in the meantime\n- A node you switched to by hand isn’t switched away within 10 minutes\n- It watches the main proxy group, the one the fallback rule uses, which is detected automatically. To watch another group, change it under Features (特色功能) → Auto-switch dead nodes (节点挂了自动换)" },
	"px-quick": { zh: "6d7399faad", q: "Is there a faster way to switch nodes?", kw: "switch node shortcut quick favorite nodes star proxy group", a: "Yes. Tap Quick (快捷) in the bottom bar. At the very bottom is Switch node (换节点), which lists one proxy group’s nodes with latency. Tap one to switch.\n\n- Tap the star left of a node name to pin favorites to the top (each phone remembers its own)\n- At the top right you can pick which proxy group to show and test latency for all\n- Nodes that are untested or failing are tested before switching, and you are asked first if the test fails\n- A node you switched to by hand isn’t switched away by “Auto-switch dead nodes” within 10 minutes\n\nWith PassWall and similar plugins, “Switch node” opens the plugin’s own node list. Family members need the “Switch nodes” permission to see it." },
	"quick-edit": { zh: "6734df7f00", q: "Can I reorder, add or remove quick actions?", kw: "quick actions customize order add remove edit open a page shortcut", a: "Yes. Tap Edit (编辑) next to Quick actions (快捷操作) on the Overview (概览) page (also available under “Quick” in the bottom bar):\n\n- Use the up and down arrows to reorder, tap ✕ to remove, and tap “Add” under “Available” to bring one back\n- “Add “Open a page””: any sidebar page can be added, including original pages, and opens with one tap\n- “Restore defaults”: back to the original layout\n\nEach phone remembers its own. Pages a family member has no permission for are hidden." },
	"px-rules": { zh: "f851623479", q: "Something broke after I changed proxy rules. Can I go back?", kw: "rules broken restore backup revert", a: "Yes. When you change rules and config files in the panel, the old version is backed up automatically before saving. The hosted edition also backs up the router settings to the cloud every day at 4:07 and keeps the latest 10, which you can restore under System (系统操作) in the panel. The current settings are backed up before restoring. Restoring brings back settings only: the panel stays on its current version, and keys such as the sign-in key and signed-in phones stay as they are now." },
	"compat-6": { zh: "2566cfd63c", q: "Will it install on my router, and which features work?", kw: "compatibility model install supported which routers features reporting privacy turn off", a: "See [Compatibility](/en/compat) on the website: which models and system versions it has actually been installed on, and how many routers each of “Remote access, One-tap update, Pause internet, Cloud backup, Full original admin page” works on. The data comes from daily anonymous router reports and lists measured results only. A model missing from the list may still install fine, it just hasn’t been reported yet.\n\nWhen a feature can’t start, the panel explains why and offers a Report this problem (报告这个问题) button with the details filled in. With “Help improve compatibility” on, the router reports the problem anonymously to the developer and, once it is fixed, pushes you a note saying which version fixes it.\n\nTo stop reporting, turn it off under System (系统操作) → Help improve, try early (帮助改进、尝鲜) in the panel. Only a random ID, the model, system version and which features work are reported, never your account, IP or settings. See the [Privacy policy](/en/privacy)." },
	"beta-6": { zh: "4bc8e2521c", q: "How do I try new versions early? Can I go back if it is buggy?", kw: "early access beta test new version try first roll back stable prerelease apply review revoke", a: "In 5.3.0 it is under System (系统操作) → Beta (尝鲜), and in 6.0 under System (系统操作) → Help improve, try early (帮助改进、尝鲜). Tap Apply (申请). A message is optional. Only the main account can apply.\n\nThe email is your website account’s, shown partly masked and not editable. For hosted routers it is the main account of this router. For self-hosted routers, tap Sign in to website account (登录官网账号), sign in on the website and tap Link (关联), and it is filled in when you return to the panel.\n\nOnce approved you get an email (hosted routers also get a push), then tap Install beta (装尝鲜版) under Check for updates (检查更新).\n\nThe request reports the model, system, version, flash, memory and your message, and the developer can’t see who you are. If it is declined or revoked, the button goes back to “Apply”, and you can apply again any time.\n\nIf something is wrong, tell us under System (系统操作) → Feedback (问题反馈). To go back, tap Back to stable (退回正式版) under “Check for updates”, with settings kept. Beta builds are signature-checked just like stable releases. To leave beta, tap Leave (退出)." },
	"up-how": { zh: "c34666bb15", q: "How do I update? Will it cut my internet?", kw: "update upgrade one-tap update new version offline", a: "When a new version is out, a small card pops up once when you open the panel. Tap One-tap update (一键更新). Each version pops up only once: this is recorded on the router, so a new phone or cleared cache won’t show it again. You can always find it later under System (系统操作) → Check for updates (检查更新) or “Notifications” (required updates are the exception and pop up every time until installed). Settings are kept and the internet stays up, though the panel disconnects briefly during the update. If the update fails it rolls back to the previous version automatically." },
	"up-must": { zh: "2db45c4ba8", q: "What does “Required update” mean?", kw: "required update forced popup security update", a: "This version includes security fixes. An update window pops up when you open the panel, and we recommend updating soon. You can see what changed in each version in the [Changelog](/en/changelog).\n\nThe hosted edition also reminds you: when a router is stuck before a required version, it sends a push to your phone and an email to the main account. Each version reminds you at most 3 times (when found, after 1 week, and 2 weeks after that), and stops once you update. To stop these emails, tap Stop reminding for this router (不再提醒这台路由器) at the bottom of the email." },
	"up-auto": { zh: "0678317677", q: "Do required updates install automatically? Can I turn that off?", kw: "automatic update auto install overnight required update turn off", a: "From 6.0, yes. Every night (between 3 and 6 a.m.) the router checks once, and if the latest version is a “Required update” (security fix) it installs it and pushes you a note. If it fails it rolls back to the previous version, and your home internet isn’t affected. Normal updates are never installed automatically, you still tap them yourself.\n\nTo stop automatic installs, turn off Install required updates automatically (必须更新自动装) under System (系统操作) → Check for updates (检查更新) in the panel (main account only). After that, required updates wait until you open the panel and tap “One-tap update”." },
	"up-old": { zh: "1c2f7b99d3", q: "I got a reminder that I need to upgrade manually once. What do I do?", kw: "manual upgrade too old one-tap update not working no response upgrade command old version", a: "On v2.0.1 and earlier, “One-tap update” in the panel doesn’t work (older versions lacked it, or it was buggy and didn’thing). Upgrade manually on the router once, and one-tap updates work from then on:\n\n1. Open My routers (我的路由器) on the website and tap Upgrade manually once · Copy command (要手动升级一次 · 复制命令) on this router\n2. With your phone on home Wi-Fi, open the router admin “Services → Terminal” (or SSH in from a computer as root), paste the command and press Enter\n3. When asked which edition to install, just press Enter (the default is what you have now) and wait for it to finish\n\nYour internet stays up, and the router address, signed-in phones and all settings are kept. No install code needed." },
	"store": { zh: "465e1c29b7", q: "Can I install plugins from the panel?", kw: "install plugin package software source feed opkg apk istore app store third-party update upgrade download", a: "Yes. Go to System (系统) → Software center (软件中心) in the panel, search or browse the list and tap Install (安装). Every software source configured on the router is detected: the firmware’s own (official), third-party sources you added, and the iStore app store. They are split by source at the top and grouped by purpose in the list (proxy, network, storage, system, themes). Space is checked first, and nothing is installed if flash is short.\n\nPlugins with new versions are listed first under Updates available (可更新). Tap Update (更新). System components (kernel, firewall, dnsmasq and so on) aren’t updated here, that needs a firmware upgrade. If a source hasn’t been refreshed in a while it says “Updated N days ago”, so tap Update software sources (更新软件源). Uninstalling is under App management (应用管理), which also handles apps installed through iStore." },
	"apps": { zh: "6c3d027ee2", q: "How do I see which plugins are installed and uninstall them?", kw: "plugins uninstall packages apps install time recently installed opkg apk remove", a: "Go to System (系统) → App management (应用管理) in the panel. It has four groups, plugins, software, dependencies and system, sorted by install time, with recent ones marked New (新装). If the router became unstable after installing a plugin, look here first.\n\nUninstall (卸载) explains the consequences before you confirm (for example, removing OpenClash stops the proxy). Items that can’t be uninstalled say why when opened: a system component, part of the firmware, needed for panel remote access, or used by another package. Only the main account can uninstall." },
	"up-safe": { zh: "1b2dc9e2a8", q: "Is one-tap update safe?", kw: "signature security tampered old version downgrade", a: "Every release is signed with the developer’s key. After downloading, the router checks the signature before installing, so a package altered in transit won’t install. One-tap update also never installs a version older than the current one (except when beta users tap “Back to stable” themselves, and that version is signature-checked too).\n\nFrom 6.0 signatures are always checked. If the router has no signature tool (usign), one-tap update installs it first (it is small). If that fails it doesn’t update and tells you what to do (install usign under System (系统) → Software (软件包) in the router admin, or update manually with the install command)." },
	"dev-manage": { zh: "24f31bce1a", q: "Can I rename devices, change their icons or delete them from the list?", kw: "device rename name icon photo delete offline clear device list", a: "Yes, on the panel Devices (设备) page:\n- **Rename**: tap the device name to edit it, and clear it to restore the original name\n- **Change icon**: tap the icon left of the name to pick a built-in icon such as phone, TV or game console, or use a photo from your gallery. Until you pick one, the panel guesses from the device name and vendor\n- **Delete**: for an offline device tap More (更多) → Remove from list (从列表删除). Clear offline devices (清除离线设备) at the top removes all offline devices you never configured in one go (devices with a pause, direct routing or a custom name are kept). Deleting also removes these settings, and the device reappears if it connects again\n\nOnline devices can’t be deleted. Names, icons and photos are stored on your router, and with cloud backup on they are encrypted and backed up like other settings. Family members need the “Parental controls” permission to change them." },
	"mon": { zh: "1110c9a563", q: "How can I tell how busy the router is?", kw: "load cpu connections conntrack lag slow busy live speed graph", a: "Go to Status (状态) → Live monitor (实时监控) in the panel, or tap the CPU and memory tile on the overview. Three graphs show speed, load and connections, updated every 2 seconds for the last 3 minutes.\n\nThe three load numbers are 1, 5 and 15 minute averages. Above the number of CPU cores (the dashed line) they turn orange, meaning the router can’t keep up. The connection count covers the whole router, and at 80% of the limit it turns red. Beyond that new connections fail. A common cause is a device doing P2P downloads." },
	"ndiag": { zh: "47630c299a", q: "How do I ping, traceroute or look up a domain?", kw: "ping traceroute domain dns nslookup latency packet loss diagnose unreachable routing table route gateway startup", a: "Go to Network (网络) → Network diagnostics (网络诊断) in the panel. Choose Ping, Traceroute or Domain lookup, enter a domain or IP (pasting a URL works too) and tap Start (开始). Everything runs from the router, wherever your phone is.\n\nPing shows average latency and packet loss. Traceroute lists every hop. Domain lookup lists the IPs found and which DNS answered. With OpenClash in Fake-IP mode the results are virtual addresses starting with 198.18, marked “Fake-IP”, which is normal. If the firmware has no traceroute, “Traceroute” is greyed out.\n\nRouting table (路由表) lists the router’s current IPv4 and IPv6 routes (destination, gateway, interface, metric), view only. Startup items are viewed and changed under Service management (服务管理)." },
	"pf": { zh: "17c0be524d", q: "How do I set up port forwarding in the panel?", kw: "port forwarding port mapping nat dnat internet access remote access nas camera public ip", a: "Go to Network (网络) → Port forwarding (端口转发) in the panel, tap Add (添加), choose the device, enter the external port (leave the internal port blank to use the same), save and tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds. If you don’t, it reverts automatically so a mistake can’t lock you out.\n\nThe ports of the router web admin, SSH and the panel can’t be forwarded, and nothing can be forwarded to the router itself. If the WAN address says “private address”, your ISP hasn’t given you a public IP, so nothing can connect in from outside. Ask your ISP for one." },
	"wan": { zh: "b3eafed755", q: "How do I change PPPoE, static IP or DNS in the panel?", kw: "internet settings broadband dial-up pppoe username password static ip dhcp dns wan isp", a: "Go to Network (网络) → Internet settings (上网设置) in the panel. Choose Automatic (自动获取), PPPoE (宽带拨号) or Static IP (固定 IP). DNS can come from your ISP or be entered yourself.\n\nAfter saving, your home internet drops briefly and the panel disconnects. Once it is back, **tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds**. If a wrong PPPoE username or password, or a wrong address, leaves the router without internet, it reverts to the previous settings by itself and pushes you a note.\n\nThe broadband password can only be changed here, not shown. To see the existing one, go to My page (我的主页) → Sensitive info (敏感信息) → Broadband credentials (宽带账号和密码), where you can view and copy it after verifying.\n\nIf choosing PPPoE says the firmware lacks the dial-up component, tap Install from software center (去软件中心装) to install ppp-mod-pppoe." },
	"lanset": { zh: "90d51bc2b7", q: "How do I change the router address (say 192.168.1.1 to 192.168.5.1) and DHCP?", kw: "LAN settings router address gateway change ip 192.168 subnet mask dhcp pool range lease lan conflict modem static ip fixed address reservation bind mac", a: "Go to Network (网络) → LAN settings (局域网设置) in the panel to change the IP address and subnet mask. DHCP can be turned on or off, with its address range and lease time. Under Fixed addresses (固定地址) you can give a device the same IP every time (adding, editing and deleting take effect right away without dropping the network). Only the main account can change the router address.\n\nChanging the router address disconnects home devices, which need to reconnect to Wi-Fi. Fixed addresses and port forwards move to the new subnet (the last number stays the same), and the address range follows.\n\nAfter saving, **tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds**:\n- If you opened the panel at home on the old address: tap “Open 192.168.5.1” on the card and tap “Keep” at the new address (no sign-in needed)\n- If you opened it from outside: reconnect Wi-Fi and tap “Keep” in the panel\n\nIf you don’t, it reverts to the previous settings. The new address can’t share a subnet with the modem, an upstream router or the guest network, and the panel will ask you to pick another." },
	"wisp": { zh: "76f585979a", q: "No cable. Can the router get internet from another Wi-Fi (wireless repeater)?", kw: "wireless repeater relay bridge wisp another wifi upstream wifi hotel dorm no cable wireless uplink", a: "Yes. Go to Network (网络) → Wireless repeater (无线中继) in the panel, choose 2.4G or 5G, tap a nearby Wi-Fi, enter its password and tap Connect (连接). Your home Wi-Fi keeps working and the router gets internet through the other one.\n\n- While connecting, your home Wi-Fi on that band drops for a few seconds. The channel is fixed and changes to match the upstream (it changes back when you disconnect the repeater)\n- After saving, **tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds**. A wrong password or a signal too weak to connect reverts automatically\n- If a cable also provides internet it takes priority, and this Wi-Fi is used only when the cable drops\n- If the upstream Wi-Fi uses the same subnet as your home (both 192.168.1.x, for example) there is no internet. The panel warns you, so change the home one under LAN settings (局域网设置)\n- Enterprise authentication and WEP can’t connect. WPA3-only networks also fail if the router’s wireless component is too old, and the list says why\n- A repeater set up in the original admin is only shown in the panel and must be changed in the original admin" },
	"traffic": { zh: "04f9e23293", q: "How is traffic counted? Does it work without a proxy plugin?", kw: "traffic stats per device usage data firewall counters PassWall offload acceleration Turbo ACC", a: "Yes. The panel’s Traffic (流量统计) counts all traffic per device using the router firewall counters, updated every minute, kept for 3 months and stored only on the router.\n\n- Proxy share: with OpenClash or Nikki, proxy and direct traffic are shown separately. With PassWall, HomeProxy and SSR Plus+ only the total is shown\n- With flow offloading (acceleration) on, it reads byte counts from connection tracking instead and turns on the kernel’s connection accounting (nf_conntrack_acct), which is switched back when the panel is uninstalled\n- With Turbo ACC, NSS, hardware NAT or similar acceleration, accelerated traffic can’t be counted and usage reads low. The traffic page tells you" },
	"rl": { zh: "d6851a9009", q: "Can I limit the speed of one device?", kw: "speed limit throttle bandwidth download speed upload speed qos one device child", a: "Yes. On the panel Devices (设备) page, tap More (更多) → Speed limit (限速) on the device, enter download and upload limits (Mbps, blank means unlimited) and save. It takes effect right away. Direct and proxied traffic together stay under the limit, and it follows the device if its IP changes.\n\n- On routers with flow offloading on, only the limited device skips acceleration, others are unaffected\n- Turbo ACC (fast forwarding), NSS or hardware NAT bypass the firewall, so limits are inaccurate and the panel warns you. For accurate limits, turn acceleration off in the original admin\n- Older firmware (fw3) needs the iptables rate-limit module (kmod-ipt-hashlimit), and the panel tells you if it is missing\n- Family members can only limit devices assigned to them" },
	"scan": { zh: "a56de6991f", q: "Some devices (printers or cameras with a manual IP) are missing from the device list?", kw: "scan deep scan missing devices device not found manual ip static ip printer camera nas", a: "Tap Scan (扫描) at the top of the Devices (设备) page. The router asks every address in your home subnet and adds devices that use a manual IP instead of DHCP. They stay in the list when offline (shown as offline) and are removed automatically after 30 days unseen.\n\nIt scans only when you tap, never on a schedule. On a very large subnet (such as 255.255.0.0) it scans only the 256 addresses around the router." },
	"oaf": { zh: "86fd3d8e4b", q: "How do I block games or video apps on one device? Can I see which apps my child used?", kw: "app filter oaf block app games video douyin tiktok parental control child usage time blocking", a: "The router needs app filtering (OAF) installed. Go to Services (服务) → App filter (应用过滤) in the panel:\n\n- Not installed: tap Install from software center (去软件中心装). If the software center can’t find it, this firmware doesn’t support it\n- Rules: tap Add (添加), give it a name, choose all devices or one, which days and hours, and which apps to block (grouped into chat, video, games and so on). Saving takes effect right away\n- Today’s usage: tap a device to see which apps it used today and for how long (main account only)\n- Older app filtering (OAF 6 and earlier) is configured in the original pages, and the panel links to it\n\nFamily members can only set rules for devices assigned to them." },
	"quota": { zh: "a7c76414ef", q: "It says “Hosted spots are full”. What now?", kw: "spots full hosted quota waitlist queue cannot sign up cannot claim trial wait", a: "The hosted service has reached its user limit, so trials and new hosted routers are paused for now. You can still sign up and sign in.\n\nTap Join waitlist (排队) under Install a new router (装新路由器) on the website account page. When a spot opens, emails go out in waitlist order, first come first served.\n\nRouters already activated keep working. You can also deploy it yourself (self-hosted), see the install guides." },
	"hot": { zh: "506ee71f2d", q: "Does the panel update itself? Will it cut my internet?", kw: "hot patch hot update automatic update silent patch offline signature V number check for updates batches rollback withdraw", a: "Yes. From 6.0, small fixes and features ship as “hot patches”: every 6 hours the router asks the website for new ones and installs them in the background. No tap needed, no restart and no internet outage. The developer’s signature is checked first, so unofficial patches are refused. Afterwards the panel checks itself and rolls back automatically if it won’t open. What each patch changed is in the website [Changelog](/en/changelog).\n\n- Don’t want to wait 6 hours: tap System (系统操作) → Check for updates (检查更新) and the router asks right away. If there is a new patch it says “Installing Vn…” and the panel refreshes itself when done\n- While the panel is open it checks announcements every 30 minutes and looks for patches at the same time\n- The “V number” after the version is the patch count, for example v6.0.0 V8\n- It doesn’t refresh while you have unsaved settings, only after you save or leave that page\n- No patches are installed during a one-tap update\n- New patches roll out in batches: beta routers first, then a share of routers, and everyone once it looks fine. The last routers get it after about 18 hours. “Check for updates” installs the latest right away\n- When the developer withdraws a patch, routers roll back by themselves\n\nMajor versions (such as 6.0 → 6.1) still use one-tap update under System (系统操作) → Check for updates (检查更新)." },
	"xpage": { zh: "730516ad84", q: "Can I open the OpenClash dashboard, AdGuard or a web terminal from outside?", kw: "remote pages openclash dashboard yacd metacubexd adguard web terminal ttyd port open outside docker", a: "Yes, under Tools (工具) → Remote pages (远程页面) in the panel, main account only. Pages the router recognizes are listed automatically, and others can be added with Add page (添加页面) and a port.\n\n- Hosted: tap Open (打开) and it opens in a new tab after a few seconds. These pages use their own address, separate from the panel’s. Only one can be open at a time, and opening another closes the previous one. They must be opened from the panel, since visiting that address directly doesn’t work\n- Local edition: opens directly on home Wi-Fi\n- No need to go through “Remote pages” every time: pages embedded in the full original admin (such as the web terminal) open in place from outside, and links inside them to other ports open in a new tab. The Dashboard (控制面板) button on the overview also opens directly from outside\n- Self-hosted: add an address in your own Cloudflare with access restrictions, see the guide docs/remote-pages.md" },
	"wg": { zh: "197e92dbb2", q: "How do I watch my home cameras or move large files when away?", kw: "wireguard wg vpn connect home encrypted tunnel camera cctv video large files nas public ip ipv6 modem port forwarding", a: "Use Tools (工具) → Encrypted tunnel (加密通道) in the panel (WireGuard). Your phone connects straight home without Cloudflare, so there are no video limits. Main account only.\n- Open “Encrypted tunnel”, tap Add phone (添加手机), confirm it is you and import by scanning with the WireGuard app. The QR code is shown only this once and can’t be seen again even on the router\n- Only the phone’s traffic to your home goes through the tunnel, and browsing still uses the phone’s own network\n- By default it reaches every home device, and you can limit it to specific devices\n- Each phone has its own key, and deleting it from the list cuts that phone off\n- Your home needs a public IP (IPv4 or IPv6). If your ISP gives you a private address (starting with 100.64), it can’t connect back. Ask your ISP for a public IP or turn on IPv6. If there is a modem above the router, forward the UDP port on the modem to this router\n- The hosted address follows your home IP automatically. Self-hosted installs use the IP, so if it changes, enter a domain of your own (dynamic DNS)\n- The router needs WireGuard installed first (luci-proto-wireguard), and the page links to it if missing" },
	"xdev": { zh: "ca1f9e51eb", q: "Can I open my home NAS or camera web pages from outside?", kw: "nas synology qnap camera cctv home devices remote access internet access open web page", a: "Yes, under Tools (工具) → Remote pages (远程页面) → Home devices (家里的设备) in the panel, main account only.\n- None are added by default. Tap Add device (添加设备), choose from devices in use at home (or enter an IP) and enter the port\n- Only devices on the home LAN can be added, not the router itself (its pages are under “Pages on the router” above) and not public addresses\n- Devices are tracked by MAC, so a changing IP is followed automatically\n- Every open sends a push to your phone and is logged in notifications\n- If a device still uses its default password, change it first\n- This is for web pages only, not for watching camera video for long periods\n- Hosted: tap “Open”. Local edition: opens directly at home. Self-hosted: see the guide docs/remote-pages.md" },
	"subupd": { zh: "2bdeba80a1", q: "After updating a subscription, can I see how much data is left?", kw: "update subscription data remaining expiry provider nikki passwall ssr homeproxy running out reminder", a: "Yes. Wherever you tap Update subscription (更新订阅) (bottom bar, quick actions, subscription page), it checks usage too and tells you how much each subscription has left and when it expires. Under 10% left or expiring within 7 days is marked Running low (快用完了).\n\nOpenClash, Nikki, PassWall, PassWall 2, SSR Plus+ and HomeProxy are all supported. Except for OpenClash, updates use the plugin’s own update script, the same as the “Update” button in its original page. When Nikki is using the subscription it restarts once after the update. If the provider doesn’t publish usage, it says so.\n\nYou don’t have to tap it yourself: the daily 9:00 health check also looks, and pushes once when a subscription has under 10% left or expires within 3 days. Each case is pushed only once, and again if it runs low after you renew." },
	"split": { zh: "c406238785", q: "Can I route a device, an app or a website through a specific line?", kw: "split routing per device per app per website direct proxy group netflix youtube chatgpt via proxy specific node override custom rules hand over to split routing subscription bundle passwall homeproxy ssr split node custom routing", a: "Yes, under Proxy (代理) → Split routing (分流) in the panel (also linked from the highlights page). It works with OpenClash, Nikki, PassWall 2, PassWall, HomeProxy and SSR Plus+, though each plugin can do different things:\n\n- OpenClash and Nikki: everything below\n- PassWall 2 and PassWall: pick nodes, route by device, website and app. The main node must be a split (分流) type. If it is not, the split routing page asks first, and only after you tap Switch to a split node (换成分流节点) does it create a split node (defaulting to your previous node) and switch to it, backing up the old settings first. Rules added by the panel go before the plugin’s own split rules. Older PassWall versions can’t route by device (their split rules have no “source”), so upgrade the plugin. Per-device routing is IPv4 only\n- HomeProxy: nodes can be picked when the routing mode is Custom routing (自定义路由). Other modes only offer direct or proxy. To pick nodes, change the routing mode to “Custom routing” in HomeProxy (DNS has to be set along with it, and the panel doesn’t change that for you). No routing by country or region\n- SSR Plus+: direct or proxy only. Addresses already on the SSR Plus+ whitelist ignore a proxy choice (the whitelist comes first)\n- With plugins other than OpenClash and Nikki, changed settings need a plugin restart and the panel asks first. If the plugin doesn’t come back within 30 seconds of a restart, the previous settings are restored, it starts again and you get a push\n\n- Destination: direct, proxy (the main group), a proxy group, or a single node (grouped by region with latency). Nodes inside subscription bundles can’t be picked, so pick the group they belong to\n- If the chosen node is down for 3 minutes, it first tries a node in the same region with the same name (differing only by number), then other nodes in the region, and if the whole region is down it waits. It switches back 10 minutes after the original recovers. The split routing page shows which node would take over and recent switches\n- Device: all traffic from the device goes to the chosen destination. Configured devices get a fixed IP automatically, and if you later change the LAN subnet the rule follows the device’s new fixed IP. With OpenClash the device’s IPv6 addresses count too, and changes are followed within 1 minute. If a phone uses a random MAC and gets a new address, you get a push to configure the new one too\n- App: common apps such as ChatGPT, Netflix, YouTube, Telegram and Bilibili, recognized by address (the router can’t see the app itself). The search box finds hundreds of apps in the website’s public table, by Chinese name, pinyin initials (such as blbl), English name or address. You can also add your own: give it a name and enter the addresses it uses\n- Website: add your own addresses, including subdomains\n- Detect apps: pick a device and open the app on it. For 3 minutes the router records the addresses it visits (IPv4 and IPv6, refreshed every second and searchable), and matches them against the website’s public “address → app” table to tell which app it is. Unrecognized ones are listed by main domain, and you can tick them to add as an app. System background addresses (connectivity checks, push, time sync) and IPs reached without the proxy are grouped separately. Main account only, because it shows which websites the device visits. The records live only in router memory and are never uploaded\n- While detecting, the router also looks at which addresses the device looked up (DNS records). With OpenClash set to “Bypass mainland China”, domestic apps going direct don’t pass through OpenClash, and this still shows their addresses. With PassWall, HomeProxy and SSR Plus+ this is the only source. dnsmasq restarts once when you tap Start (开始) and once at the end, so home DNS pauses for under a second. Only this device’s entries are read, kept in memory and deleted at the end. If that line is in /etc/dnsmasq.d instead, dnsmasq is left alone: OpenClash still sees its own connections, while PassWall and similar plugins can’t detect apps, so add them by hand under Website (网站). Only this device’s entries are read, kept in memory and deleted at the end. Nikki and OpenClash with firewall DNS forwarding don’t use this (dnsmasq can’t see the queries)\n- “Direct IPs” under detect apps: apps that connect to an IP without a DNS lookup, such as apps using HTTPDNS (many Chinese apps), where the router sees only the IP\n- Country and region: no new ones from 6.0. Existing ones still apply and can be set back to follow the global setting in the “Country/region” column, which is hidden if you never used it\n- Family: under My page (我的主页) → Family (家人) → Manage (管理), turn on All their devices go direct (他的设备都不走代理), and all devices assigned to them (including ones claimed later) go direct\n- What you wrote in overrides: OpenClash custom rules and Nikki rules not added by the panel are also listed in split routing, marked From override (覆写里的). When they clash with split routing, yours win. To manage one in split routing, tap it and then Hand over to split routing (交给分流管): those lines are removed from the override (the original file is backed up first) and take effect after a restart. Keyword and IP range rules can’t be managed by split routing and stay in the override\n\nFor each connection, device rules come first, then website and app rules. Adding a new kind of destination needs one OpenClash or Nikki restart. A Restart now (现在重启) prompt appears at the top and it restarts only when you tap it. If a chosen proxy group disappears after a subscription update, it falls back to the main group and pushes you a note.\nIf the OpenClash custom rules are rewritten wholesale in the original admin or by an AI, the split routing and “direct” lines are added back automatically. Changes by the AI are fixed on the spot. Changes in the original admin are fixed within 1 minute with a push, and take effect after OpenClash restarts." },
	"fwup": { zh: "5d05bece99", q: "Can I upgrade firmware or factory reset from my phone?", kw: "firmware upgrade flash sysupgrade factory reset reset defaults firstboot upgrade system", a: "Yes, under System (系统) → Firmware upgrade (固件升级) in the panel. Main account only, and only on home Wi-Fi (the buttons are greyed out when away).\n\nIf you are on home Wi-Fi but it says it didn’t recognize your home Wi-Fi, your phone is probably reaching the panel through a proxy node. Tap Open with home address (用家里地址打开) next to it to jump to the panel at “http://router-address:906”, with no password, and do it there.\n\n- Firmware upgrade: pick a firmware file (the sysupgrade kind). The phone uploads it into router memory, and the router checks it matches this model before allowing the upgrade. “Keep settings” is the default, and the panel is kept too. The internet is down for 3–5 minutes during the upgrade\n- Factory reset: all settings are erased and the panel is removed too, so it must be reinstalled\n\nBoth require a backup first (the full edition backs up to the cloud; without cloud, download one to your phone, and it must be from the last 30 minutes), and finally the router admin password." },
	"weekly": { zh: "9717cdb07b", q: "What is the weekly report? Can I turn it off?", kw: "weekly report summary week outages top traffic new devices push", a: "Every Monday at 9:10 you get a push with last week’s report: how many outages (the longest, and why), how many automatic node switches, the three devices with the most traffic, and newly connected devices (names only, no IPs).\n\nTo stop it, turn off Weekly report (每周报告) under Features (特色功能) → Alerts and backup (提醒和备份) in the panel." },
	"move": { zh: "6e179d7230", q: "I got a new router. Can I move the panel settings over?", kw: "move router replacement new router migrate transfer settings switch transfer code old router", a: "Yes (hosted), under Tools (工具) → Switch routers (换路由器) in the panel, main account only.\n- On the old router, tap Package this router’s settings (打包这台路由器的设置) and copy the move code\n- Once the panel is installed on the new router and bound to the same account, paste the code on the same page, tap View (查看), check it and tap Move here (搬过来)\n- Moved: device names and owners, direct routing, pauses and internet schedules, speed limits, schedules, split routing, automatic node switching, remote pages and highlight toggles. Tick Bring family too (家人一起转过来) to move family members and their permissions to the new router as well\n- Not moved: Wi-Fi, router address and internet connection type (the page lists the old router’s settings so you can set them on the matching pages)\n- Rules are keyed by device MAC, so they still match on the new router. Direct routing and split routing switch to the IPs the new router assigns\n- A move code lasts 24 hours and works once, and packaging again invalidates the old one. It can move only to a router of the same main account\n- Settings are encrypted with the key inside the move code before being stored on the website, so the website can’t read them\n- Self-hosted installs use “Cloud backup” and restore on the new router" },
	"svcsw": { zh: "7d2d211742", q: "How do I turn file sharing (Samba), FTP, SSH or the router LEDs on and off from my phone?", kw: "samba smb file sharing shared folder nas hard drive usb ftp vsftpd ssh dropbear port key password login led lights off too bright", a: "Under System (系统) → Common services (常用服务) in the panel. Main account only.\n\n- File sharing: Samba 4, Samba 3.6 and ksmbd are supported. Add share (添加共享) picks an attached hard drive or USB stick. There is no password, any device on the home LAN can open it, and it can’t be reached from the internet. Only folders under /mnt and /media can be shared, and deleting a share doesn’t delete files\n- FTP: you get a warning before turning it on. FTP is unencrypted and the username and password travel in plain text, so use it only at home\n- SSH: change the port, allow LAN only, or turn off password login. Password login can’t be turned off until an SSH key is added (otherwise you would be locked out). Turning SSH off doesn’t affect the panel\n- LEDs: turn them all off with one tap, and they stay off after a reboot. Turn them back on to restore how they were\n\nAnything the firewall exposes to the internet is marked Reachable from the internet (外网能连). Missing services offer Install from software center (去软件中心装), or say they aren’t in the software sources." },
	"sched": { zh: "2dbf6f8617", q: "Can the router restart on a schedule or turn Wi-Fi off at night? Can it shut down on a timer?", kw: "scheduled restart scheduled tasks turn off wifi at night timed shutdown power off auto reboot", a: "Under Features (特色功能) → Schedules (定时) in the panel:\n\n- Scheduled restart: choose days and a time (such as 04:00 every day). It skips a restart within 20 minutes of booting, to avoid restart loops\n- Scheduled Wi-Fi off: choose days and when to turn it off and on (such as off at 23:30, on at 07:00). If the router gets internet through the wireless repeater, it doesn’t turn off (that would cut the internet)\n\nOnly the main account can set these, and times follow the router’s time zone.\n\nTimed shutdown isn’t possible because most routers can’t power themselves back on. To shut down, tap Shut down (关机) under System (系统操作), and unplug and replug the power to turn it back on." },
	"dev-wifi": { zh: "f4cf4d3384", q: "Can I change the Wi-Fi name and password in the panel? What if I can’t reconnect?", kw: "Wi-Fi WiFi wireless name SSID password change hidden channel 2.4G 5G dual band revert cannot connect keep", a: "Yes, under Network (网络) → Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi) in the panel: name, password, hidden name and channel. 2.4G and 5G can be turned on and off separately or share one name and password.\n\nNew settings apply as soon as you save, and devices on this Wi-Fi disconnect and need to reconnect with the new name or password. It only sticks if you **return to the panel and tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds**. If you don’t (say you made a mistake and can’t reconnect), the router reverts to the previous settings by itself and pushes you a note.\n\n- Passwords that are too easy to guess (12345678, one repeated character, sequential digits) are refused\n- Radar channels (52–144) can’t be chosen for 5G: switching to one means waiting 1–10 minutes before use, which wouldn’t reconnect within 90 seconds\n- Only the home network Wi-Fi is changed, not guest, repeater or Mesh networks. Enterprise (802.1X) passwords are changed in the original admin\n- Family members need “Full control” to view and change it" },
	"dev-guest": { zh: "dae151a0f9", q: "Is guest Wi-Fi safe? Does it turn off by itself?", kw: "guest visitor QR code scan isolation expiry auto off temporary Wi-Fi", a: "Turn it on at the bottom of Network (网络) → Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi) in the panel and choose 2 hours, 1 day or 7 days. It turns off automatically when time is up and pushes you a note. Each time it is turned on it gets a new password, and guests connect by scanning the QR code.\n\n- Guests use a separate network: internet only, no access to your home devices or the router admin, and guests can’t see each other\n- Guests use public DNS and skip the router’s proxy plugin (direct)\n- Both 2.4G and 5G are turned on (same name and password), or just the one band if there is only one\n- The first time, a separate network is added for guests and home devices drop for a few seconds. Tap Keep (保留) within 90 seconds, or it is undone automatically\n- Some routers can’t do it: if the wireless driver isn’t mac80211 (some closed-source MTK drivers, for example) or there are no firewall or DHCP settings, the panel explains why. If the wireless chip can’t run two Wi-Fi networks at once, you are told which band didn’t come up" },
	"dev-plan": { zh: "070742ab53", q: "Can I set internet time for my child’s tablet?", kw: "child internet time schedule time slots weekdays weekend timer offline extend parent tablet game console screen time", a: "Yes. On the panel Devices (设备) page, tap your child’s device → More (更多) → Internet schedule (上网计划) and add allowed time slots by weekday (for example Monday to Friday 16:00–21:00, weekends 09:00–22:00). Outside them it goes offline automatically. Times follow the router clock.\n\n- **Reminder before time is up**: 10 minutes before cutoff, the parent who set the schedule gets a push (or every phone with notifications on, if that parent’s phone has them off). Open it to extend by 30 minutes or 1 hour. The button on the push only opens the panel, and it takes effect after tapping again in the panel\n- **Recognized even with a new MAC**: if a new device shows up with the same device name, you get a push and can apply the schedule to it too. It is best to turn off the phone’s “Private address” (random MAC) in the Wi-Fi settings on the child’s device\n- While offline the device stays on Wi-Fi but can’t reach any websites. Family members need the “Parental controls” permission to set schedules and extend time" },
	"help-fb": { zh: "27da5bb25b", q: "How do I contact the developer about a problem or a feature idea?", kw: "feedback contact support developer feature request suggestion", a: "Feedback (问题反馈) is at the bottom of the panel sidebar and of the home page. You can attach screenshots and files and send them straight to the developer, or use Chat with developer (实时联系开发者) in the panel. You get a ticket number after sending feedback." },
	"help-track": { zh: "91aadd52ac", q: "How do I track my feedback after sending it?", kw: "progress ticket number lookup status reply", a: "Use the ticket number: enter the 8-character number under “Check feedback status” on the website home page, no sign-in needed. You can also check under Help (帮助) → My feedback (我的反馈) in the panel or on the [account page](/app)." },
	"help-files": { zh: "8c13d76710", q: "How large can files be, and how long are they kept?", kw: "files size video upload how long delete", a: "“Chat with developer” and hosted “Feedback” accept videos, documents and archives, up to 5 at a time and 200 MB each. Files you send are deleted automatically after 30 days, and only you and the developer can open them." },
	"help-heic": { zh: "53f4436298", q: "Can I send iPhone HEIC photos?", kw: "HEIC HEIF iPhone photo Apple format cannot open screenshot", a: "Yes. Feedback screenshots, images in developer chat, device photos and avatars all accept HEIC. Browsers on iPhone convert to JPG automatically. When you pick a .heic file from an iPhone on Android or a computer, the panel first downloads a converter (about 1.3 MB, only once) and converts it to JPG on your phone before sending. If the download fails, pick the photo directly on the iPhone, or use a screenshot instead." },
	"help-sec": { zh: "f50a071e9b", q: "How do I report a security issue?", kw: "security vulnerability report abuse privacy", a: "Sign in to your website account first, then use the form at the bottom of the [Security](/en/security#report) page. Progress updates go to your account email and also show under My feedback (我的反馈) on the account page." },
};
